      "claim": "True salmon (Salmo salar and Oncorhynchus spp.) are anadromous and spawn only in freshwater.",
      "evidence": "Standard ichthyology texts (e.g., \"Biology of Salmonids\") and peer‑reviewed studies describe salmon egg deposition and fertilisation occurring exclusively in freshwater gravel beds.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": []
